"""Dictator helper: records the microphone and turns speech into text on this computer.

Started by the Dictator GNOME extension for each recording. It records with pw-record until it gets
"stop" or "cancel" on stdin ("pause" / "resume": the paused stretch is cut out) and turns it into text
with a speech model in a sandbox without network: Small (tinyasr language packs, run by the dictate-tinyasr
worker built from engine/; the default) or Large (NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6B v3, parakeet.py). The recording
is transcribed in pieces cut at your pauses WHILE you speak (class Streamer), so the text is there about a
second after you stop, however long you spoke.
Protocol on stdout, one line each:
    L <0..1>      voice level, ~20 per second while recording
    S             recording finished, transcribing
    T <json str>  the text
    E <message>   error (English, shown on screen)

The recording is kept in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dictate (RAM) until its text is out; a failed one stays there
and `dictate --retry` transcribes it again. With the history on (privacy settings) the last 3
recordings stay in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dictate-history for the extension's menu. Kept recordings are
deleted after keep_minutes. Nothing is written to the disk but settings, the model and a log of numbers
(~/.cache/dictate/dictate.log, never any text). This program never touches the clipboard.

Other commands:
    dictate --models               installed models, as JSON (for the settings window)
    dictate --download int8|fp32   download a Large model variant from Hugging Face (pinned revision, every
                                   file checked against its SHA-256)
    dictate --download small[:PACK]
                                   download Small model language packs from GitHub (pinned commit, every
                                   file checked against its SHA-256): PACK, or the packs for your languages
                                   The --download commands are the only network access.
    dictate --remove int8|fp32     delete a model variant
    dictate --remove small:PACK    delete a language pack (the last one takes the Small model with it)
    dictate --try                  a test dictation (the settings window): like a recording, but
                                   nothing is kept, neither the audio nor the text
    dictate --selftest             load the model (and Small too, if installed) once and check that its
                                   sandbox has no network
    dictate --redo STAMP [LANG]    transcribe a recording from the history again (its audio is kept only
                                   with keep_audio on), as LANG or with the usual languages; prints S, then
                                   T or E, and the new text replaces the old one in the history

Where the Large model runs: ~/.config/dictate/runtime holds "host" (system Python with onnxruntime + numpy,
in bubblewrap) or "podman" / "docker" (the offline "dictate-asr" image built from Containerfile).
Without that file: host if those Python packages are installed, else podman, else docker.
The Small model always runs on this computer, in bubblewrap (else not at all).
"""
